    "explanation": "Cross-checked the screenshot filename/path (bug_screenshot_1.png, /app/.harbor_assets/...) across instruction.md, Dockerfile, ASSET_MANIFEST.json, and evidence_bundle.json — all consistent. No spelling errors or broken identifiers found in instruction.md, task.toml, test.patch, or the bug patches."
  },
  "tests_or_solution_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The Dockerfile only COPYs environment/assets/bug_screenshot_1.png into the image; it explicitly does not COPY tests/ or solution/, and comments in the Dockerfile confirm this is intentional ('tests/ and solution/ are intentionally NOT copied into the image -- the harness supplies them at verify time')."
  },
  "test_deps_in_image": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "test.sh explicitly states the verify run is offline and installs nothing; it only relies on the TypeScript compiler already present in the image via the target repo's own `npm install`, which is a project dependency rather than a test-only addition."
  },
  "hardcoded_solution": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "solution/solve.sh applies solution/fix.patch, a genuine multi-file source diff (Base.ts parameter-threading, ModifiableValue.ts ceil/sort fixes, helpers.ts duplicate() restoration) mirroring the real upstream fix commit — it performs the actual code change rather than printing or injecting a precomputed answer."
  },
  "file_reference_mentioned": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "The task does not require the agent to produce new named output files (e.g. output.csv) for the tests to check; it requires modifying existing source files discovered through codebase exploration, so there is no output filename that needs to be stated in instruction.md."
  }
}

